0
00:00:07,379 --> 00:00:09,247
PREVIOUSLY ON...

1
00:00:09,247 --> 00:00:10,949
NNENNA GAVE
HER JEALOUS BOYFRIEND...

2
00:00:10,949 --> 00:00:12,918
Nnenna, did you kiss
on a guy?

3
00:00:12,918 --> 00:00:15,520
SOMETHING TO WORRY ABOUT.

4
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:17,289
BROOKE FLOUNDERED
AT THE PHOTO SHOOT.

5
00:00:17,289 --> 00:00:18,356
DOES THIS LOOK GOOD?

6
00:00:18,356 --> 00:00:19,524
DOES IT SELL AN OUTFIT?

7
00:00:19,524 --> 00:00:20,559
OKAY.

8
00:00:20,559 --> 00:00:21,960
WHILE FURONDA TOOK CONTROL.

9
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:23,462
IT'S GOOD.

10
00:00:23,462 --> 00:00:25,230
AND EVEN THOUGH GINA
CONFRONTED JADE...

11
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:27,232
YOU CAN SAY WHATEVER
THE HELL YOU WANT, JADE.

12
00:00:27,232 --> 00:00:29,334
SHE LET IT AFFECT
HER PERFORMANCE ON SET

13
00:00:29,334 --> 00:00:30,802
AND AT JUDGING.

14
00:00:30,802 --> 00:00:32,504
IT'S NOT PERFECT WHERE
WE'RE LIVING RIGHT NOW,

15
00:00:32,504 --> 00:00:33,972
AND I'M LETTING IT GET TO ME,
OBVIOUSLY.

16
00:00:33,972 --> 00:00:35,440
IN THE END,
GINA WAS SENT HOME.

17
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,675
NINE GIRLS REMAIN.

18
00:00:36,675 --> 00:00:38,643
WHO WILL BE ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

19
00:00:38,643 --> 00:00:42,547
♪♪♪

20
00:01:26,324 --> 00:01:28,560
GINA WAS IN THE BOTTOM TWO
THAT ONE WEEK. SHE GOT TO STAY.

21
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:29,561
THE NEXT WEEK, SHE'S GONE.

22
00:01:29,561 --> 00:01:30,562
YEAH.

23
00:01:30,562 --> 00:01:31,563
I WAS IN THE BOTTOM TWO
THIS WEEK.

24
00:01:31,563 --> 00:01:32,664
THE NEXT WEEK,
I'M GONNA BE GONE.

25
00:01:32,664 --> 00:01:33,799
NO.

26
00:01:33,799 --> 00:01:35,700
WHAT DO I KNOW?
I'M NOT TYRA.

27
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:37,769
I WAS IN THE BOTTOM TWO

28
00:01:37,769 --> 00:01:40,605
BECAUSE TYRA TELLS ME THAT
I HAVE ALL THIS POTENTIAL,

29
00:01:40,605 --> 00:01:42,774
BUT I CANNOT TAKE
A GOOD PHOTOGRAPH.

30
00:01:42,774 --> 00:01:45,977
BUT ALL THE JUDGES SEE
RIGHT NOW IS POTENTIAL.

31
00:01:45,977 --> 00:01:47,512
BYE-BYE, BROOKEY.

32
00:01:47,512 --> 00:01:48,947
LIKE, I ALMOST WANNA GO
INTO PANEL AND BE, LIKE,

33
00:01:48,947 --> 00:01:51,483
"BEFORE YOU SAY ANYTHING,
LET ME SHOW YOU SOME MOLLIE."

34
00:01:51,483 --> 00:01:53,451
TYRA'S BEEN TELLING ME IN PANEL,

35
00:01:53,451 --> 00:01:54,920
LIKE, "JUST SHOW US
YOUR PERSONALITY."

36
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:57,455
THE JUDGES AREN'T GETTING
A SENSE OF WHO YOU ARE.

37
00:01:57,455 --> 00:02:00,458
MY PERSONALITY IS SO MUCH
A PART OF ME, AND, LIKE,

38
00:02:00,458 --> 00:02:01,459
NO ONE'S SEEING IT.

39
00:02:01,459 --> 00:02:02,561
"MOLLIE'S ALWAYS GOOFY.

40
00:02:02,561 --> 00:02:04,663
SHE MAKES FUNNY FACES.
SHE FARTS."

41
00:02:04,663 --> 00:02:06,464
BUT YOU CAN'T PLAN ANYTHING,
EITHER,

42
00:02:06,464 --> 00:02:07,899
'CAUSE THAT'S WHEN I GO,
"DUH, DUH, DUH."

43
00:02:07,899 --> 00:02:08,900
NNENNA'S ON THE PHONE.

44
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,802
SHOOT, DUDE.

45
00:02:10,802 --> 00:02:13,438
I WENT TO SLEEP LAST NIGHT

46
00:02:13,438 --> 00:02:14,973
REALLY, REALLY DEPRESSED,
AND THAT'S NOT FAIR.

47
00:02:14,973 --> 00:02:16,208
Oh, yeah?

48
00:02:16,208 --> 00:02:17,409
Well, think about how I felt

49
00:02:17,409 --> 00:02:18,844
every night so far this month.

50
00:02:18,844 --> 00:02:21,479
JOHN IS INSECURE
ABOUT CERTAIN THINGS

51
00:02:21,479 --> 00:02:23,849
BECAUSE WE HAD A PHOTO SHOOT
WITH A MALE MODEL.

52
00:02:23,849 --> 00:02:25,917
ALL RIGHT, NNENNA.

53
00:02:25,917 --> 00:02:27,586
Don't do this to me.

54
00:02:27,586 --> 00:02:28,653
I know something's up.

55
00:02:28,653 --> 00:02:30,722
I know it, all right?

56
00:02:30,722 --> 00:02:32,190
OKAY, JOHN, JOHN.
I DON'T WANT TO ARGUE ANYMORE.

57
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:33,491
THIS HAS GONE DIRTY ENOUGH.

58
00:02:33,491 --> 00:02:35,594
IT'S ENOUGH.
ENOUGH IS ENOUGH.

59
00:02:35,594 --> 00:02:39,297
I DO CARE ABOUT HIM,
BUT I ALSO WANT TO KEEP MY FOCUS

60
00:02:39,297 --> 00:02:41,333
FOR WHAT I'M HERE FOR.

61
00:02:41,333 --> 00:02:43,268
I'M DONE. DONE.

62
00:02:43,268 --> 00:02:44,269
RELATIONSHIP IS OVER.

63
00:02:44,269 --> 00:02:45,270
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

64
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:46,271
IT'S OVER.

65
00:02:46,271 --> 00:02:47,639
OH, MY GOD.

66
00:02:47,639 --> 00:02:49,908
I DON'T HAVE A BOYFRIEND.
I'M FREE.

67
00:02:49,908 --> 00:02:51,877
I HAVE NOTHING HOLDING ME BACK.

68
00:02:51,877 --> 00:02:54,412
SO I LOVE HER TO DEATH,

69
00:02:54,412 --> 00:02:57,716
BUT THAT'S GONNA HURT HER
IN THE END.

70
00:03:00,185 --> 00:03:01,453
YOU FEEL WHAT I'M SAYING?

71
00:03:01,453 --> 00:03:03,822
JADE IS THE TYPE OF PERSON--

72
00:03:03,822 --> 00:03:05,790
IF SHE FEELS LIKE SHE'S FOUND
AN EASY TARGET,

73
00:03:05,790 --> 00:03:08,627
SHE WORKS THAT FOR AS MUCH
AS SHE CAN WORK IT FOR,

74
00:03:08,627 --> 00:03:09,928
LIKE SHE DID WITH GINA.

75
00:03:09,928 --> 00:03:11,663
HERE, JUST KISS IT. COME ON.
KISS IT, KISS IT.

76
00:03:11,663 --> 00:03:14,266
NO, IT'S OKAY.

77
00:03:14,266 --> 00:03:15,567
THERE ARE A LOT OF PEOPLE

78
00:03:15,567 --> 00:03:18,603
THAT ARE NOT WHAT THEY SAY
OR NOT WHAT THEY SEEM.

79
00:03:18,603 --> 00:03:19,905
I DON'T THINK YOU SHOULD
BREAK UP WITH HIM.

80
00:03:19,905 --> 00:03:21,306
BUT THEN AGAIN,
I'M NOT IN YOUR RELATIONSHIP.

81
00:03:21,306 --> 00:03:22,374
I DON'T KNOW.

82
00:03:22,374 --> 00:03:23,375
YEAH, I THINK JADE KNOWS.

83
00:03:23,375 --> 00:03:24,376
SHE KNOWS WHAT SHE'S DOING.

84
00:03:24,376 --> 00:03:25,810
WHAT GOES AROUND COMES AROUND.

85
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:28,546
SHE'S PLAYING A GAME TOO MUCH.

86
00:03:28,546 --> 00:03:31,650
♪♪♪

87
00:03:31,650 --> 00:03:32,751
HELLO!

88
00:03:32,751 --> 00:03:34,185
HI!

89
00:03:34,185 --> 00:03:35,387
HOW IS EVERYBODY?

90
00:03:35,387 --> 00:03:36,554
GOOD.

91
00:03:36,554 --> 00:03:38,490
ANY PRESSURE, ANYTHING?

92
00:03:38,490 --> 00:03:40,859
WHAT'S THE HARDEST PART
OF BEING IN THIS COMPETITION?

93
00:03:40,859 --> 00:03:41,660
NOT KNOWING WHAT'S
GONNA HAPPEN NEXT.

94
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:42,861
REALLY?

95
00:03:42,861 --> 00:03:45,196
WELL, YOU GUYS ARE THE TOP NINE,

96
00:03:45,196 --> 00:03:46,932
SO YOU'VE GOTTEN THIS FAR.

97
00:03:46,932 --> 00:03:49,935
SO IS IT HARD WALKING
INTO THE JUDGING ROOM AND...

98
00:03:49,935 --> 00:03:53,338
YES.

99
00:03:53,338 --> 00:03:53,939
I'VE BEEN WORKING SO HARD.

100
00:03:53,939 --> 00:03:55,473
I'M SO TIRED, YOU GUYS.

101
00:03:55,473 --> 00:03:56,908
I FEEL...

102
00:03:56,908 --> 00:03:58,677
I'M SO SORRY, YOU GUYS.

103
00:03:58,677 --> 00:04:00,512
I DON'T MEAN TO BE
ALL WEAK IN FRONT OF YOU,

104
00:04:00,512 --> 00:04:03,682
BUT I'M JUST SO LIGHT-HEADED.

105
00:04:03,682 --> 00:04:05,450
SOMEBODY BRING SOME WATER.

106
00:04:05,450 --> 00:04:06,484
GET SOME PIZZA?

107
00:04:06,484 --> 00:04:07,886
SOME JUICE.

108
00:04:07,886 --> 00:04:09,721
I'M ALL RIGHT.

109
00:04:09,721 --> 00:04:11,356
NO! TYRA!

110
00:04:11,356 --> 00:04:15,293
TYRA! PLEASE SAVE HER, Y'ALL!

111
00:04:15,293 --> 00:04:16,828
OH, MY GOD.

112
00:04:16,828 --> 00:04:17,729
WHAT'S HER PULSE?

113
00:04:17,729 --> 00:04:19,397
CHECK HER PULSE.

114
00:04:23,201 --> 00:04:26,905
I'M ALL RIGHT. I'M OKAY.

115
00:04:29,441 --> 00:04:31,876
TODAY YOU GUYS
ARE GONNA LEARN ABOUT ACTING!

116
00:04:31,876 --> 00:04:33,445
LEARN ABOUT ACTING!

117
00:04:33,445 --> 00:04:34,813
ACTING! ACTING! ACTING!

118
00:04:34,813 --> 00:04:35,947
THAT WAS FAKE!

119
00:04:35,947 --> 00:04:37,248
THAT WAS A GOOD JOB.

120
00:04:37,248 --> 00:04:39,718
GOOD JOB.

121
00:04:39,718 --> 00:04:41,886
THAT WAS A GOOD JOB.

122
00:04:41,886 --> 00:04:45,724
OH... ARE YOU OKAY?

123
00:04:45,724 --> 00:04:48,426
I CAN'T DEAL WITH IT.

124
00:04:48,426 --> 00:04:50,829
I THINK TYRA'S
TOO GOOD OF AN ACTRESS,

125
00:04:50,829 --> 00:04:53,832
AND THAT WAS A VERY MEAN TRICK
THAT SHE PLAYED ON US.

126
00:04:53,832 --> 00:04:56,267
WELL, I DID THAT BECAUSE
YOU GUYS ARE GONNA BE LEARNING

127
00:04:56,267 --> 00:04:59,704
ALL ABOUT ACTING THIS WEEK,
AND IT'S ABOUT BEING CONVINCING,

128
00:04:59,704 --> 00:05:00,872
AND IT'S ABOUT BEING REAL.

129
00:05:00,872 --> 00:05:02,507
YOU HAVE TO BE ABLE

130
00:05:02,507 --> 00:05:04,342
TO BE IN
A COMMERCIAL AND SAY THE WORDS

131
00:05:04,342 --> 00:05:06,511
AND BE CONVINCING, ALL RIGHT?

132
00:05:06,511 --> 00:05:08,613
SO THAT IS WHY I DID THIS,

133
00:05:08,613 --> 00:05:12,283
TO SHOW YOU GOTTA GO FOR IT,
AND YOU GOTTA COMMIT.

134
00:05:12,283 --> 00:05:14,386
TO MAKE UP FOR
WHAT I JUST DID TO YOU,

135
00:05:14,386 --> 00:05:16,221
I HAVE THESE SHIRTS FOR YOU.

136
00:05:16,221 --> 00:05:17,789
THIS IS A LITTLE GIFT FROM ME.

137
00:05:17,789 --> 00:05:18,857
THANK YOU!

138
00:05:18,857 --> 00:05:20,825
I WANT ALL OF YOU GUYS
TO SHINE.

139
00:05:20,825 --> 00:05:22,794
I WANT ALL OF YOU GUYS
TO BE GOOD ACTRESS-MODELS

140
00:05:22,794 --> 00:05:25,764
AND MAKE
YOUR LITTLE MAMA PROUD.

141
00:05:25,764 --> 00:05:26,698
SEE YA LATER!

142
00:05:26,698 --> 00:05:27,966
BYE!

143
00:05:27,966 --> 00:05:29,434
OH, MY GOODNESS.

144
00:05:29,434 --> 00:05:31,336
I CANNOT ACT.

145
00:05:31,336 --> 00:05:33,238
'CAUSE I'M SO GULLIBLE.

146
00:05:33,238 --> 00:05:36,341
♪♪♪

147
00:05:38,443 --> 00:05:39,577
HI, GUYS.
WELCOME TO THE GROUNDLINGS.

148
00:05:39,577 --> 00:05:40,845
I'M JEREMY ROWLEY.

149
00:05:40,845 --> 00:05:42,680
THIS IS AN IMPROV
AND SKETCH THEATER.

150
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,815
FROM THIS THEATER HAVE COME

151
00:05:43,815 --> 00:05:46,418
A LOT OF
REALLY SUCCESSFUL PERFORMERS

152
00:05:46,418 --> 00:05:48,787
LIKE WILL FERRELL,
LISA KUDROW,

153
00:05:48,787 --> 00:05:50,688
JENNIFER COOLIDGE,
PEE-WEE HERMAN.

154
00:05:50,688 --> 00:05:51,956
THIS IS COOL.

155
00:05:51,956 --> 00:05:54,259
LIKE, FAMOUS PEOPLE THAT
ARE ON TV HAVE ORIGINATED HERE.

156
00:05:54,259 --> 00:05:55,460
WE HAVE A LOT OF
DIFFERENT PEOPLE

157
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:58,563
TAKE OUR CLASSES,
INCLUDING TYRA BANKS.

158
00:05:58,563 --> 00:05:59,864
AND SHE'S PERFORMED
ON THIS VERY STAGE

159
00:05:59,864 --> 00:06:01,633
AS A CELEBRITY GUEST.

160
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:04,369
I ALWAYS WANTED TO TAKE
A PROFESSIONAL ACTING LESSON.

161
00:06:04,369 --> 00:06:06,438
GIRL, I THINK I'M MADE
FOR THIS STAGE.

162
00:06:06,438 --> 00:06:08,873
TODAY YOU'RE GOING TO BE
DOING SOME IMPROV GAMES

163
00:06:08,873 --> 00:06:11,776
AND EXERCISES,
AND WE'RE GONNA HELP YOU

164
00:06:11,776 --> 00:06:13,278
LET YOUR PERSONALITY
COME THROUGH.

165
00:06:13,278 --> 00:06:14,712
I WAS REALLY EXCITED ABOUT IT

166
00:06:14,712 --> 00:06:17,415
JUST 'CAUSE THIS IS GONNA
HELP ME IN PANEL.

167
00:06:17,415 --> 00:06:18,650
THEY'RE GOING TO SEE
THAT I'M A GOOFBALL

168
00:06:18,650 --> 00:06:20,452
WITHOUT THEM GOING,
"WHAT IS SHE DOING?"

169
00:06:20,452 --> 00:06:22,520
I'M JUST GONNA ASK YOU
TO KIND OF THROW YOURSELF

170
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:25,824
INTO THE THING I ASK YOU TO DO
AND NOT JUDGE THE RESULT.

171
00:06:25,824 --> 00:06:27,492
TERRIFIED! GO!

172
00:06:27,492 --> 00:06:29,394
(screaming)

173
00:06:29,394 --> 00:06:30,695
EXCELLENT!
AND NOW YOU'RE JANICE DICKINSON!

174
00:06:30,695 --> 00:06:31,763
HOLLA!

175
00:06:31,763 --> 00:06:32,764
GO!

176
00:06:32,764 --> 00:06:37,268
(screeching)

177
00:06:37,268 --> 00:06:38,236
ANGER!
KEEP MOVING AS YOU DO IT!

178
00:06:38,236 --> 00:06:42,507
(shouting)

179
00:06:42,507 --> 00:06:43,708
BACK TO NEUTRAL WALKING.

180
00:06:43,708 --> 00:06:44,943
GOOD. THAT ONE WAS EASY.

181
00:06:44,943 --> 00:06:46,678
ANGER WAS EASY, HUH?

182
00:06:46,678 --> 00:06:49,647
SIMPLE EXERCISE LIKE THAT
IS GONNA HELP YOU

183
00:06:49,647 --> 00:06:51,683
WITH YOUR MODELING.

184
00:06:51,683 --> 00:06:54,185
PEOPLE ARE GONNA ASK YOU TO DO
SOME REALLY INTERESTING THINGS

185
00:06:54,185 --> 00:06:55,753
IN A MODELING SHOOT,

186
00:06:55,753 --> 00:06:57,489
AND THEY'RE GONNA WANT YOU
TO COMMIT TO IT.

187
00:06:57,489 --> 00:06:59,557
CAN'T BE LIKE, "THIS IS CRAZY.
THIS IS STUPID," RIGHT?

188
00:06:59,557 --> 00:07:02,260
NEXT THING WE'RE GONNA DO,
YOU'RE GONNA WORK AS A TEAM.

189
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:05,463
WE'RE GONNA
CREATE A STORY TOGETHER.

190
00:07:05,463 --> 00:07:07,866
OKAY, THIS IS CALLED
"ONE NIGHT STAND."

191
00:07:07,866 --> 00:07:11,736
DOMINIQUE WALKED
INTO THE NICE, WARM BEDROOM.

192
00:07:11,736 --> 00:07:14,272
IMPROV WORRIES ME BECAUSE
YOU HAVE TO COME UP WITH THINGS

193
00:07:14,272 --> 00:07:16,708
LIKE, OUT OF NOWHERE,
AND WHEN I'M PUT ON THE SPOT,

194
00:07:16,708 --> 00:07:18,676
I BECOME REALLY NERVOUS.

195
00:07:18,676 --> 00:07:21,246
WHERE HE SLATHERED BUTTER
ALL OVER LAMAR.

196
00:07:21,246 --> 00:07:23,481
LITTLE MORE ENERGY,
MOLLIE SUE.

197
00:07:23,481 --> 00:07:25,483
"THE PRINCESS AND HER DOGGIE."

198
00:07:25,483 --> 00:07:28,286
(British accent)
THE PRINCESS' MOM
SAID THAT WALKING HER DOG

199
00:07:28,286 --> 00:07:29,821
IS A DELIGHTFUL TREATMENT.

200
00:07:29,821 --> 00:07:31,489
(foreign accent)
SHE WALKED HER DOG,
AND ONE DAY,

201
00:07:31,489 --> 00:07:34,926
HE BECAME MAGICALLY INCLINED
TO TELL HER...

202
00:07:34,926 --> 00:07:36,728
NOT WHILE SHE'S TALKING.

203
00:07:36,728 --> 00:07:39,631
YOUR MOMENT INTERRUPTED
THE STORY, AND ALL OF A SUDDEN,

204
00:07:39,631 --> 00:07:41,466
THE STORY DOESN'T
MAKE SENSE ANYMORE, RIGHT?

205
00:07:41,466 --> 00:07:44,736
SOMETIMES IT'S NOT ABOUT YOU.

206
00:07:44,736 --> 00:07:47,572
ALL RIGHT, LADIES,
I HOPE THAT THESE LESSONS

207
00:07:47,572 --> 00:07:49,541
WILL CARRY WITH YOU,
AND YOU'LL USE SOME OF

208
00:07:49,541 --> 00:07:51,976
THESE LITTLE TIPS AND TRICKS
WITH YOU OUT THERE,

209
00:07:51,976 --> 00:07:53,211
SO THANKS VERY MUCH.

210
00:07:53,211 --> 00:07:54,279
GET OUT OF HERE.

211
00:07:54,279 --> 00:07:55,480
(laughter)

212
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,247
- THANK YOU.
- THANKS FOR COMING.

213
00:07:57,782 --> 00:07:59,284
Nnenna, here's the problem.

214
00:07:59,284 --> 00:08:01,319
HONEY, ENOUGH IS ENOUGH.
I NEED SOME SUPPORT.

215
00:08:01,319 --> 00:08:03,621
I NEED TO BE MENTALLY PREPARED
AND WELL RESTED.

216
00:08:03,621 --> 00:08:06,925
NNENNA HAS HAD NOTHING
BUT DRAMA WITH HER BOYFRIEND.

217
00:08:06,925 --> 00:08:08,193
I'm on the edge right now.

218
00:08:08,193 --> 00:08:09,761
YOU'RE EMBARRASSING ME.

219
00:08:09,761 --> 00:08:10,962
HE'S CRYING ALL THE TIME.

220
00:08:10,962 --> 00:08:12,864
(crying)

221
00:08:12,864 --> 00:08:14,832
SHE'S SCREAMING AT HIM.

222
00:08:14,832 --> 00:08:17,669
SO GET UP, JOHN. SERIOUSLY.

223
00:08:17,669 --> 00:08:19,404
STOP.

224
00:08:19,404 --> 00:08:20,538
I THINK IT'S BROUGHT OUT

225
00:08:20,538 --> 00:08:21,673
A KIND OF A NEGATIVE SIDE
OF NNENNA.

226
00:08:21,673 --> 00:08:23,541
YOU'RE ALREADY CRYING,
AND IT'S ANNOYING

227
00:08:23,541 --> 00:08:24,576
AND MAKING ME ANGRY.

228
00:08:24,576 --> 00:08:25,944
No, I wasn't crying.

229
00:08:25,944 --> 00:08:28,346
IT'S MAKING ME ANGRY INSTEAD
OF MAKING ME SYMPATHETIC.

230
00:08:28,346 --> 00:08:31,182
I'M ONLY GONNA HATE YOU
WHEN I GET BACK, I SWEAR TO GOD.

231
00:08:31,182 --> 00:08:32,517
I'M TRYING TO BE FAIR.

232
00:08:32,517 --> 00:08:37,722
JADE IS ADVISING NNENNA
TO, YOU KNOW, STAY WITH HER MAN.

233
00:08:37,722 --> 00:08:38,856
"YOU NEED TO TRUST ME."

234
00:08:38,856 --> 00:08:40,390
YOU NEED TO TRUST ME, JOHN.

235
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:41,960
